From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topology: publish neighbor-added convergence events

An expired IEEE1905 neighbor is reported to the higher-layer entity, but the
same neighbor being learned again is retained only inside the IEEE1905
topology database.  Periodic Topology Responses are consumed by IEEE1905 and
do not necessarily reach the EasyMesh controller.  The controller can
therefore keep a live, responding agent suppressed after it rejoins.

Publish a topology-change event whenever received evidence creates a new
IEEE1905 neighbor.  Send the normal multicast Topology Notification and its
local AL-SAP indication just as for removal.  This lets the higher-layer
controller issue its standard bounded Topology Query and restore the same
logical agent without polling or implementation-specific network messages.

Extend the expiry regression to prove the initial add and post-expiry re-add
events are both published exactly once.

Upstream-Status: Pending
